  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Prol.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> Prol.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol.">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">Þis syndan þa gerædnessa þe Engla rædgifan gecuran ⁊ gecwædan ⁊ geornlice lærdan þæt man scolde healdan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">These are the ordinances which the councillors of England have decided and agreed upon, earnestly enjoining that they should be observed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Prolog. Dies sind die Satzungen, welche die [Staats]räthe der Engländer erkoren und erklärt und ernstlich angewiesen haben, dass sie gehalten werden sollen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Prologue. These are the ordinances which the councillors [of state] of the English have chosen and declared and earnestly instructed are to be kept.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares V Atr Prol.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
